WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.340
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:00.440 --> 00:00.940
Hey!

3
00:00.970 --> 00:02.220
You two are cops, aren't you?

4
00:02.320 --> 00:02.800
You...

5
00:11.130 --> 00:11.750
Let go of me!

6
00:11.860 --> 00:13.350
Your eyebrow is bleeding.

7
00:13.400 --> 00:14.050
Are you alright?

8
00:14.070 --> 00:14.740
I'm fine.

9
00:14.880 --> 00:16.080
Die, you bastards!

10
00:16.760 --> 00:17.490
Inspector,

11
00:17.510 --> 00:18.670
stop blaming yourself.

12
00:18.890 --> 00:21.050
Mungkorn might even be happy when he wakes up

13
00:21.080 --> 00:23.170
and realizes you...

14
00:23.190 --> 00:25.600
care about him like you're in love with him.

15
00:25.630 --> 00:28.340
I'm your love, Inspector Thear?

16
00:56.510 --> 00:57.200
Perfect.

17
01:21.700 --> 01:22.470
Hey, Thear.

18
01:26.710 --> 01:28.450
What are you doing at Mungkorn's desk?

19
01:29.580 --> 01:32.580
Well, he left his desk a bit messy,

20
01:32.610 --> 01:34.980
so I'm just helping him tidy up. That's all.

21
01:36.840 --> 01:42.360
Right, give me a summary of the Black Bull case tonight.

22
01:43.840 --> 01:45.310
Can I hand it in tomorrow instead?

23
01:46.160 --> 01:48.890
I happen to have some important business to take care of today.

24
01:50.180 --> 01:52.340
I have to be at the hospital to look after Mungkorn.

25
01:52.740 --> 01:55.120
It won't be good if I'm late.

26
01:56.320 --> 01:57.080
Basically,

27
01:58.720 --> 02:00.260
it's not about the business,

28
02:00.900 --> 02:02.910
but the person.

29
02:03.980 --> 02:07.640
Well, that explains why you're taking such good care of him.

30
02:09.630 --> 02:12.890
Mungkorn is lucky. He's got a great boss...

31
02:12.920 --> 02:15.450
and a wonderful husband.

32
02:17.860 --> 02:19.000
Wait a minute, Uncle.

33
02:19.680 --> 02:20.780
Do you...

34
02:21.080 --> 02:22.760
know about us?

35
02:24.960 --> 02:28.870
If I couldn't figure that out, how could I be the chief around here?

36
02:30.410 --> 02:31.150
Okay.

37
02:31.890 --> 02:33.060
Then get going.

38
02:33.700 --> 02:36.570
We can talk about the summary some other time.

39
02:38.120 --> 02:39.510
Your partner is waiting.

40
02:41.940 --> 02:43.090
He's not just any partner.

41
02:44.970 --> 02:45.910
He's my husband.

42
02:49.080 --> 02:49.720
I see...

43
03:11.000 --> 03:11.920
Whoa!

44
03:12.690 --> 03:15.160
See what happens when you don't let me go undercover as a host?

45
03:15.480 --> 03:16.900
That's how you ended up getting shot.

46
03:17.710 --> 03:18.960
Stop bragging so much.

47
03:18.980 --> 03:20.390
You got yourself hurt, too.

48
03:21.850 --> 03:23.080
I let my guard down.

49
03:23.530 --> 03:25.050
Let's just call it a lesson learned.

50
03:26.650 --> 03:27.830
Anyway, at the very least,

51
03:28.480 --> 03:31.400
we caught a whole bunch of those Black Bull agents.

52
03:31.800 --> 03:33.440
But we still haven't gotten their boss.

53
03:33.950 --> 03:35.690
That Tiannan guy we caught...

54
03:35.960 --> 03:37.200
is just another underling.

55
03:38.600 --> 03:39.460
I'm not giving up.

56
03:40.730 --> 03:41.820
No matter what,

57
03:42.510 --> 03:45.050
I have to track them all the way to the boss.

58
03:45.670 --> 03:46.630
Just take it easy.

59
03:52.360 --> 03:53.750
Don't push yourself too hard.

60
03:54.170 --> 03:55.720
Wait until you're fully recovered first.

61
03:56.160 --> 03:57.210
I'll take care of him.

62
03:59.030 --> 04:00.600
I just hate to let the trail go cold.

63
04:01.310 --> 04:03.680
I feel like we're getting closer every minute.

64
04:06.620 --> 04:07.480
It's not going to be easy.

65
04:08.010 --> 04:10.240
These people have connections everywhere.

66
04:12.850 --> 04:14.150
They could even have someone in here.

67
04:16.160 --> 04:17.490
Is it you, Kanin?

68
04:17.890 --> 04:18.980
Watch what you're saying.

69
04:19.400 --> 04:20.780
I almost got caught myself,

70
04:20.980 --> 04:22.660
so I had to kiss Nadol to fool those guys.

71
04:25.620 --> 04:26.420
- You guys kissed? - You guys kissed?

72
04:26.830 --> 04:29.720
We did it just to throw them off,

73
04:29.990 --> 04:32.420
just like how you two tricked Tiannan.

74
04:32.450 --> 04:33.270
It's pretty much the same.

75
04:41.690 --> 04:43.000
You'd better watch out for this one

76
04:43.620 --> 04:45.080
because Kanin was serious about it.

77
04:50.540 --> 04:51.390
I actually didn't mind.

78
04:52.530 --> 04:53.590
Well, I certainly did.

79
04:55.730 --> 04:58.430
Keep bickering, and you might actually end up together.

80
04:58.840 --> 04:59.860
I've seen it happen before.

81
05:05.700 --> 05:06.800
I'll go get the door.

82
05:15.440 --> 05:16.370
Saming?

83
05:18.330 --> 05:19.270
What are you doing here?

84
05:22.390 --> 05:23.160
Why?

85
05:24.050 --> 05:25.810
Can't I visit my friend?

86
05:43.080 --> 05:46.060
(Yin as Theartha)

87
05:50.990 --> 05:53.720
(War as Mungkorn)

88
05:57.860 --> 06:00.210
(Shane as Phuwin)

89
06:00.640 --> 06:03.680
(Boss as Lukplub)

90
06:06.060 --> 06:07.790
(Kit as Kanin)

91
06:08.050 --> 06:10.000
(Tang as Nadol)

92
06:13.480 --> 06:18.720
(Tae as Saming)

93
06:44.990 --> 06:46.210
How are you doing, Mungkorn?

94
06:46.640 --> 06:48.100
When I heard that you'd been shot,

95
06:48.120 --> 06:49.770
I rushed here immediately.

96
06:50.130 --> 06:51.770
Thank you so much for coming,

97
06:51.850 --> 06:53.690
but I'm feeling a lot better now.

98
06:53.970 --> 06:56.090
You shouldn't have troubled yourself to come all this way.

99
06:56.370 --> 06:57.410
It's necessary.

100
06:57.630 --> 06:59.150
I was worried sick about you.

101
07:00.220 --> 07:02.850
I wonder how the inspector here takes care of his men

102
07:03.280 --> 07:04.800
when he lets one of them nearly get killed.

103
07:06.810 --> 07:09.070
Mungkorn, if you were under my wing,

104
07:09.380 --> 07:13.000
I guarantee you wouldn't have a single scratch on you.

105
07:14.290 --> 07:15.540
That's not what happened.

106
07:16.110 --> 07:18.020
I should have been more careful myself.

107
07:18.270 --> 07:22.510
As a cop, you know these things can happen.

108
07:23.640 --> 07:24.400
It's okay.

109
07:25.390 --> 07:27.070
Let me take care of you right now, then.

110
07:27.700 --> 07:28.430
Here.

111
07:28.890 --> 07:31.270
I brought you plenty of stuff to help you recover.

112
07:35.390 --> 07:36.400
I don't think that's necessary.

113
07:36.780 --> 07:38.890
Mungkorn can feed himself. He doesn't need your help.

114
07:38.920 --> 07:39.920
I know,

115
07:40.380 --> 07:42.070
but I still want to do it for him.

116
07:42.790 --> 07:44.070
It's not your job.

117
07:44.090 --> 07:45.270
Then whose job is it?

118
07:45.630 --> 07:46.560
Is it yours?

119
07:47.260 --> 07:48.210
And why is it yours?

120
08:01.750 --> 08:02.540
It's fine, guys.

121
08:03.120 --> 08:04.190
I'll eat it myself.

122
08:23.380 --> 08:24.460
It's really sweet.

123
08:27.290 --> 08:28.290
Totally organic.

124
08:30.890 --> 08:33.010
Here, I bought you some coffee.

125
08:35.190 --> 08:35.990
Thank you.

126
08:41.950 --> 08:42.800
Captain,

127
08:43.130 --> 08:45.260
how come Inspector Saming from Phayao

128
08:45.630 --> 08:47.140
knows Mungkorn?

129
08:47.570 --> 08:50.090
From what I heard, back when they were students,

130
08:50.200 --> 08:53.650
Thear and Saming were senior volunteers who served as assistant trainers.

131
08:54.020 --> 08:55.880
That was exactly the year Mungkorn joined.

132
08:57.660 --> 08:59.610
Everyone, right face!

133
09:07.660 --> 09:09.660
He seems genuinely worried about Mungkorn, though.

134
09:10.710 --> 09:13.370
Maybe he just wants to mess with Thear.

135
09:13.390 --> 09:13.890
Sh*t.

136
09:18.170 --> 09:19.430
- You bastard! - Cut it out!

137
09:19.660 --> 09:21.120
Why are you guys fighting?

138
09:25.200 --> 09:26.900
Phuwin told me that

139
09:26.920 --> 09:28.410
they've been rivals forever.

140
09:33.150 --> 09:34.910
But let's not mind them.

141
09:35.420 --> 09:36.930
Let's focus on us instead.

142
09:37.640 --> 09:38.550
What are you talking about?

143
09:39.050 --> 09:40.950
I'm talking about the fact that you kissed me.

144
09:42.370 --> 09:43.230
What about it?

145
09:43.250 --> 09:45.780
I told you it was just for the mission.

146
09:46.530 --> 09:47.900
Why are you making a big deal out of it?

147
09:48.520 --> 09:49.320
Whoa...

148
09:49.660 --> 09:51.350
You kissed me, and now you're ditching me?

149
09:51.870 --> 09:53.300
Why are you being so dramatic?

150
09:53.630 --> 09:54.680
I'm not.

151
09:55.200 --> 09:56.750
But since our lips have met,

152
09:56.770 --> 09:58.570
I'm considering you off the market.

153
10:00.020 --> 10:01.610
Whatever you say, Captain.

154
10:33.620 --> 10:35.550
(Why didn't you tell me, sweetie?)

155
10:35.580 --> 10:39.430
(Would you have kept it from me if Saming hadn't told me?)

156
10:39.460 --> 10:41.730
I just didn't want you to worry, Mom.

157
10:41.750 --> 10:44.940
(I'm coming to stay with you until you're better.)

158
10:44.970 --> 10:46.480
You don't need to, Mom.

159
10:46.610 --> 10:48.680
It's a long way. It'll be too much trouble for you.

160
10:50.220 --> 10:51.620
Don't worry, Mom.

161
10:51.830 --> 10:53.730
I'll look after Mungkorn for you.

162
10:54.000 --> 10:55.530
(Thank you, Saming.)

163
10:55.710 --> 10:57.080
(I'm counting on you.)

164
10:57.230 --> 10:59.960
(Can I talk to Inspector Thear for a second?)

165
11:02.490 --> 11:03.290
Thear.

166
11:04.000 --> 11:04.750
What?

167
11:06.310 --> 11:08.090
Mungkorn's mom wants to talk to you.

168
11:11.670 --> 11:13.810
You should leave so Mungkorn can get some rest.

169
11:24.390 --> 11:25.370
Hello, Mom.

170
11:26.130 --> 11:27.000
(Inspector...)

171
11:27.490 --> 11:29.510
(Why didn't you tell me...)

172
11:29.700 --> 11:31.500
(about Mungkorn being shot?)

173
11:32.060 --> 11:32.860
Oh...

174
11:35.080 --> 11:37.130
Mungkorn asked me not to.

175
11:37.160 --> 11:38.540
He was worried you'd be upset.

176
11:38.570 --> 11:40.300
(That's still not right.)

177
11:40.320 --> 11:42.040
(He's my only son.)

178
11:42.180 --> 11:44.840
(I allowed my son to marry you,)

179
11:45.020 --> 11:47.290
(so you must take good care of him.)

180
11:47.490 --> 11:50.130
(Mungkorn is my heart.)

181
11:50.420 --> 11:52.610
(You have to look after him)

182
11:52.960 --> 11:55.080
(as if you were looking after your own heart.)

183
11:55.110 --> 11:56.410
- Had to get it removed. - (Do you understand?)

184
11:57.050 --> 11:58.250
Of course, Mom.

185
11:58.950 --> 12:00.100
From now on,

186
12:00.380 --> 12:02.780
I will protect Mungkorn with my life.

187
12:29.150 --> 12:30.700
This is so frustrating.

188
12:31.160 --> 12:32.210
So annoying.

189
12:32.240 --> 12:33.760
If you keep sighing like that,

190
12:34.440 --> 12:35.860
you're going to die young,

191
12:36.400 --> 12:38.080
since you're not exactly young anymore.

192
12:38.240 --> 12:40.900
Fine, just let me die.

193
12:46.820 --> 12:47.480
Hey.

194
12:48.300 --> 12:49.920
What's wrong, Inspector?

195
12:53.340 --> 12:54.480
What did you just call me?

196
12:55.320 --> 12:56.470
Inspector...

197
12:57.780 --> 12:58.880
What did you say?

198
12:59.270 --> 13:00.150
Inspector.

199
13:01.050 --> 13:02.970
If you don't call me what you used to,

200
13:04.290 --> 13:06.890
I'll let out the biggest sigh the whole world can hear.

201
13:12.120 --> 13:13.520
Thear!

202
13:14.370 --> 13:15.440
Happy now?

203
13:17.760 --> 13:18.780
I guess so.

204
13:22.840 --> 13:24.910
So, why all the sighing?

205
13:25.650 --> 13:28.740
Did my mom say something to upset you?

206
13:29.290 --> 13:30.080
No.

207
13:30.590 --> 13:31.880
She didn't say anything bad.

208
13:32.790 --> 13:34.440
She just told me to take good care of you.

209
13:34.870 --> 13:36.260
Since I've married her son,

210
13:36.390 --> 13:38.740
I have to look after both his life and his heart.

211
13:42.180 --> 13:44.220
My mom is just overprotective.

212
13:45.080 --> 13:46.460
Don't overthink it.

213
13:50.120 --> 13:51.430
But that's not the point.

214
13:55.660 --> 13:57.050
Then what is it?

215
13:59.770 --> 14:00.900
It's you.

216
14:01.570 --> 14:03.000
Ever since Saming showed up,

217
14:03.020 --> 14:04.360
I've been cast aside like a stray dog.

218
14:04.580 --> 14:06.210
Why were you so happy to see him?

219
14:06.870 --> 14:07.700
Well...

220
14:08.210 --> 14:10.230
I haven't seen him in such a long time.

221
14:10.750 --> 14:11.750
Should I have been scowling?

222
14:12.310 --> 14:13.170
I had to smile.

223
14:13.810 --> 14:14.640
Whatever you say,

224
14:14.670 --> 14:17.620
but was it really necessary to let him feed you fruit like that?

225
14:18.080 --> 14:19.610
If he's feeding me, I have to...

226
14:19.970 --> 14:20.990
I have to eat it.

227
14:23.210 --> 14:24.650
You want me to swat it away?

228
14:25.830 --> 14:27.200
Whoa.

229
14:27.400 --> 14:28.660
Always taking his side, huh?

230
14:28.680 --> 14:30.050
You never agree to anything I say.

231
14:36.230 --> 14:36.970
Look.

232
14:38.230 --> 14:41.140
Are you being jealous or just mad?

233
14:43.230 --> 14:44.190
That's right.

234
14:44.410 --> 14:45.090
I'm jealous.

235
14:45.400 --> 14:46.350
Very jealous.

236
14:47.880 --> 14:48.980
My husband...

237
14:49.090 --> 14:50.430
I can take care of him myself.

238
14:52.890 --> 14:53.590
Hey.

239
14:54.570 --> 14:55.710
- Ow... - Whoa, whoa.

240
14:56.050 --> 14:57.050
Sorry. Did I hit it?

241
14:57.130 --> 14:58.050
I'm okay.

242
15:01.250 --> 15:02.660
I just wanted to say...

243
15:02.950 --> 15:04.480
it doesn't matter what others think.

244
15:04.510 --> 15:05.640
I don't care.

245
15:06.310 --> 15:07.910
I'm married,

246
15:08.280 --> 15:10.550
and the only one I care about is you, Thear.

247
15:17.470 --> 15:19.220
You're staying here tonight.

248
15:20.440 --> 15:22.680
You're distracted right now. I can't let you go home alone.

249
15:22.700 --> 15:25.410
You'll probably end up back in the hospital somehow.

250
15:25.930 --> 15:27.230
Your mom will be worried.

251
15:31.700 --> 15:33.050
I have one small problem.

252
15:33.110 --> 15:35.460
It's cold sleeping on the couch.

253
15:37.960 --> 15:40.050
Then sleep on the bed. I'll sleep on the couch.

254
15:40.740 --> 15:41.610
Just kidding.

255
15:42.730 --> 15:43.570
It's fine.

256
15:43.590 --> 15:46.610
Just being able to look at your face is enough to keep me warm.

257
15:48.110 --> 15:49.280
Couch it is.

258
15:57.120 --> 15:57.990
Are you sure?

259
15:58.540 --> 15:59.390
Would you be alright?

260
15:59.520 --> 16:00.220
It's fine.

261
16:00.650 --> 16:02.100
Slowly.

262
16:42.570 --> 16:43.550
What are you doing?

263
16:44.050 --> 16:45.070
A sponge bath?

264
16:45.560 --> 16:46.510
Yes.

265
16:46.930 --> 16:48.470
Please let me do it, then.

266
16:49.350 --> 16:50.700
What are you talking about?

267
16:51.210 --> 16:53.680
Let the nurse do it. It's her job.

268
16:53.720 --> 16:56.290
But as your husband, it's my job

269
16:56.610 --> 16:58.350
to take care of you when you're not well.

270
17:00.140 --> 17:00.710
Isn't that right?

271
17:00.850 --> 17:01.940
Yes, that's right.

272
17:02.070 --> 17:02.970
Exactly.

273
17:03.870 --> 17:05.530
In that case, please go ahead.

274
17:06.490 --> 17:07.760
I'll just leave things as they were.

275
17:07.780 --> 17:08.460
Okay.

276
17:09.340 --> 17:10.220
Please, go ahead.

277
17:10.240 --> 17:12.350
- Thank you so much. - You're welcome.

278
17:13.430 --> 17:14.550
I feel like a third wheel.

279
17:15.760 --> 17:16.730
I've got you a flower

280
17:17.140 --> 17:18.010
to brighten things up.

281
17:19.320 --> 17:20.230
Thank you.

282
17:23.310 --> 17:24.950
Oh, are you shy around me?

283
17:27.540 --> 17:29.410
I've already seen all of you.

284
17:30.880 --> 17:31.930
I know.

285
17:32.820 --> 17:34.480
Anyway, I'm still not used to it.

286
17:36.390 --> 17:37.620
You'd better get used to it

287
17:38.520 --> 17:39.830
because from now on,

288
17:40.200 --> 17:42.270
I'm going to give you a sponge bath every single day

289
17:42.480 --> 17:43.890
until you're fully recovered.

290
19:23.800 --> 19:25.460
I'm going to lift it slowly.

291
19:26.960 --> 19:28.070
How's this?

292
19:36.180 --> 19:36.770
It hurts?

293
19:37.630 --> 19:38.850
Is it okay if I keep going?

294
19:38.900 --> 19:40.470
- Keep going, Inspector. - Okay.

295
19:40.690 --> 19:41.320
Here we go!

296
19:44.130 --> 19:45.940
Hang in there. Look at me. Stay strong.

297
19:46.430 --> 19:47.500
Okay, all the way!

298
19:50.370 --> 19:51.740
Take deep breaths, Mungkorn.

299
19:54.580 --> 19:55.390
Can you handle it?

300
19:55.950 --> 19:56.680
Yeah.

301
19:56.840 --> 19:57.640
How does it feel?

302
19:58.170 --> 19:59.580
- Relaxing? - We should change positions.

303
19:59.850 --> 20:00.940
- Let's try another one. - Oh...

304
20:03.620 --> 20:05.590
This is a hospital. What are you doing?

305
20:07.150 --> 20:08.020
Just some stretching.

306
20:08.760 --> 20:09.280
Right...

307
20:10.600 --> 20:12.270
- Oh, okay. - No worries. Thank you very much.

308
20:12.290 --> 20:13.320
You can just leave it there.

309
20:13.710 --> 20:14.790
Here's your evening medication.

310
20:14.850 --> 20:15.960
Yes, thank you.

311
20:16.000 --> 20:16.800
- Thank you. - You're welcome.

312
20:18.680 --> 20:19.800
Shall we keep going?

313
20:19.830 --> 20:20.500
Yes.

314
20:21.350 --> 20:22.390
Bend your knee for this one.

315
20:22.570 --> 20:23.650
Bend your knee.

316
20:25.780 --> 20:26.440
Listen.

317
20:26.940 --> 20:27.900
It hurts, doesn't it?

318
20:29.540 --> 20:30.210
It does.

319
20:39.590 --> 20:40.430
Oh, hey.

320
20:40.700 --> 20:41.520
How are you feeling?

321
20:41.950 --> 20:43.090
Ready to get back to work?

322
20:43.140 --> 20:43.770
Yes, sir.

323
20:43.990 --> 20:46.060
I am Sergeant Mungkorn Phianwanich,

324
20:46.170 --> 20:48.230
ready to serve the people!

325
20:49.530 --> 20:50.870
Whoa, what's all this?

326
20:51.770 --> 20:53.360
Is the wound opening up?

327
20:53.960 --> 20:54.910
Let me see.

328
20:57.650 --> 20:58.800
It doesn't hurt too much, does it?

329
20:58.870 --> 20:59.710
No, it's fine.

330
21:00.690 --> 21:02.050
Let's not play around just yet.

331
21:02.330 --> 21:03.440
Your wound has only just healed.

332
21:03.480 --> 21:04.370
Understood.

333
21:08.650 --> 21:09.770
Thank you, Thear,

334
21:10.290 --> 21:11.970
for looking after me for the last three weeks.

335
21:15.430 --> 21:16.330
Well, I told you

336
21:16.990 --> 21:19.320
that I'm the perfect husband.

337
21:41.110 --> 21:42.820
All healed up, right?

338
21:43.330 --> 21:46.450
You can continue your recovery at home

339
21:46.480 --> 21:49.220
as we're out of ant killer at the hospital.

340
21:49.240 --> 21:51.960
Apparently, the ants couldn't handle all this sweetness.

341
21:52.600 --> 21:54.650
Thank you so much, Miss Pretty Nurse.

342
21:54.780 --> 21:55.350
You're welcome.

343
21:55.540 --> 21:57.110
Come on. Let's go.

344
22:00.300 --> 22:01.490
Let's go.

345
22:01.950 --> 22:02.980
- Goodbye. - Thank you.

346
22:03.010 --> 22:03.910
- Thank you. - My pleasure.

347
22:10.040 --> 22:12.570
Must be nice to be so good-looking and loved.

348
22:14.100 --> 22:15.140
My goodness.

349
22:24.540 --> 22:26.650
Wait, aren't we going back to our place?

350
22:26.970 --> 22:28.390
My, my.

351
22:28.900 --> 22:31.210
Are you already comfortable calling my house "our place"?

352
22:32.030 --> 22:32.830
I'm so happy.

353
22:33.670 --> 22:35.720
I brought you here to keep my promise.

354
22:36.060 --> 22:37.320
I said if you made it through,

355
22:37.400 --> 22:39.500
we'd come have shaved ice at your favorite place.

356
22:41.380 --> 22:43.480
Actually, the place is closed today,

357
22:44.290 --> 22:45.980
but I booked the whole place out

358
22:46.100 --> 22:47.350
just for you.

359
22:47.840 --> 22:48.860
Are you for real?

360
22:49.670 --> 22:51.270
You went to all that trouble?

361
22:51.680 --> 22:52.800
For you...

362
22:53.190 --> 22:54.690
I'd do even more.

363
22:58.370 --> 22:59.720
Come on, let's eat.

364
23:09.790 --> 23:10.990
- Hello! - Hello.

365
23:11.020 --> 23:12.270
What would you like today?

366
23:12.820 --> 23:14.510
I'll have the grass jelly, sugar palm seeds,

367
23:14.540 --> 23:17.570
and a mix of red and green syrups with lots of condensed milk, please.

368
23:17.650 --> 23:18.300
Coming right up.

369
23:18.320 --> 23:19.250
Whoa,

370
23:19.330 --> 23:21.160
adding all these extras and lots of condensed milk?

371
23:21.740 --> 23:23.560
Are you really that deprived of sweetness?

372
23:24.010 --> 23:25.730
I thought I'd given you enough of that already.

373
23:26.250 --> 23:27.860
Guess it's still not enough.

374
23:28.230 --> 23:30.520
I'll have to be your personal sugar factory, then.

375
23:31.350 --> 23:32.610
This is plenty.

376
23:32.930 --> 23:33.970
I don't want to end up with diabetes.

377
23:35.470 --> 23:36.570
We'll take two, please.

378
23:36.930 --> 23:39.080
Would you like anything else?

379
23:39.590 --> 23:41.010
No, I'm good.

380
23:41.820 --> 23:44.020
What about this one? Don't you want him?

381
23:46.110 --> 23:46.940
This one...

382
23:47.990 --> 23:49.830
He'd take it home with him.

383
23:50.970 --> 23:52.430
Did you tell her to say that?

384
23:52.720 --> 23:53.540
What do you mean?

385
23:53.990 --> 23:55.740
She can see for herself that we're a couple.

386
23:56.290 --> 23:57.300
She's just teasing us.

387
23:57.780 --> 23:58.790
Isn't that right?

388
23:59.080 --> 23:59.930
That's right.

389
24:00.220 --> 24:01.420
No need to be shy.

390
24:07.870 --> 24:08.580
Ow!

391
24:09.330 --> 24:09.930
What's wrong?

392
24:11.730 --> 24:12.860
Brain freeze.

393
24:14.150 --> 24:16.530
You ate it too fast. That's why you got a brain freeze.

394
24:17.770 --> 24:19.570
Is it really that good?

395
24:20.060 --> 24:21.230
Did you have to eat it that quickly?

396
24:22.210 --> 24:23.210
It is good.

397
24:23.670 --> 24:25.260
It makes me feel so much better.

398
24:25.630 --> 24:26.750
When I was in the hospital,

399
24:27.290 --> 24:28.640
I had to eat the same food every day.

400
24:32.780 --> 24:34.290
If there's anything you want to eat

401
24:34.470 --> 24:35.530
or anywhere you'd like to go,

402
24:35.820 --> 24:36.860
just let me know.

403
24:37.410 --> 24:39.520
I took the day off today specifically to take care of you.

404
24:40.490 --> 24:41.620
Come on, Thear.

405
24:42.080 --> 24:43.910
I can take care of myself now.

406
24:44.310 --> 24:46.390
I know you can,

407
24:46.670 --> 24:47.900
but I want to do it for you.

408
24:48.900 --> 24:50.550
Come on, just let me.

409
24:53.080 --> 24:53.840
Fine.

410
24:56.780 --> 24:59.030
So, is there anywhere you want to go?

411
25:00.130 --> 25:00.880
Yeah.

412
25:01.450 --> 25:02.950
I want to go to a temple and pay my respects.

413
25:03.310 --> 25:05.450
I've been having some seriously bad luck lately.

414
25:06.760 --> 25:07.340
Alright.

415
25:07.520 --> 25:09.170
Let's go make merit together,

416
25:09.890 --> 25:10.990
and from now on,

417
25:11.190 --> 25:13.030
we'll both be lucky.

418
25:27.610 --> 25:28.590
Are you doing okay?

419
25:28.860 --> 25:30.150
It's still quite a long way.

420
25:30.940 --> 25:32.730
You should've taken the cable car like I told you to.

421
25:34.190 --> 25:35.750
No need. I'm fine.

422
25:35.870 --> 25:36.750
After all,

423
25:37.190 --> 25:39.430
I need to get some exercise.

424
25:39.940 --> 25:40.810
Are you sure you're fine?

425
25:41.050 --> 25:41.670
Yeah.

426
25:41.690 --> 25:43.510
- Let me carry you up. - No way, stop it.

427
25:43.730 --> 25:44.660
I'll walk by myself.

428
25:48.910 --> 25:50.110
Whoa, whoa!

429
25:54.920 --> 25:55.650
See?

430
25:56.170 --> 25:57.270
I told you so.

431
25:57.550 --> 25:58.420
You're not going to make it.

432
25:58.460 --> 25:59.660
Let me help you up.

433
26:01.290 --> 26:02.090
Fine, then.

434
26:06.740 --> 26:07.440
So stubborn.

435
26:10.830 --> 26:12.820
If I fell from here, I'd break my neck.

436
26:17.210 --> 26:19.850
My name is Theartha Phiromsamorn.

437
26:20.220 --> 26:22.670
My name is Mungkorn Phianwanich...

438
26:23.250 --> 26:25.010
- From this day forward, - From this day forward...

439
26:29.750 --> 26:33.120
may there be no more hardship or harm in our lives.

440
26:33.850 --> 26:35.430
May we never get hurt again.

441
26:36.030 --> 26:40.470
And may we live happily for many years to come.

442
27:09.120 --> 27:10.100
What's wrong?

443
27:10.510 --> 27:11.800
I stepped on a lit incense stick.

444
27:13.350 --> 27:14.380
Let's go sit down first.

445
27:19.260 --> 27:21.130
- Hang in there. Take a seat. - Ow, it stings!

446
27:22.510 --> 27:23.450
It burns!

447
27:24.010 --> 27:25.010
Let me have a look.

448
27:27.170 --> 27:28.180
It's really red.

449
27:32.260 --> 27:33.230
Let's cool it down first...

450
27:35.550 --> 27:37.310
so it won't blister too badly.

451
27:38.340 --> 27:39.250
Thank you.

452
27:43.900 --> 27:44.590
How are you feeling?

453
27:44.930 --> 27:46.610
Will you be able to walk down?

454
27:46.640 --> 27:47.920
I'm fine. Look, it's gone.

455
27:48.140 --> 27:49.410
Whoa, seriously?

456
27:52.240 --> 27:53.520
I stepped right on it.

457
27:57.380 --> 28:01.030
Seeing you kids so in love really warms my heart.

458
28:03.230 --> 28:04.170
By the way,

459
28:04.830 --> 28:06.420
I've got a story to tell you.

460
28:06.830 --> 28:09.440
There's a legend about this place.

461
28:10.070 --> 28:11.600
What kind of legend, sir?

462
28:12.040 --> 28:14.140
The legend says...

463
28:14.820 --> 28:16.850
if a couple isn't meant to be

464
28:16.870 --> 28:19.800
and they come up here to worship at Doi Suthep,

465
28:21.200 --> 28:23.150
they'll end up breaking up once they go back down.

466
28:24.260 --> 28:26.350
Why do people believe that?

467
28:27.430 --> 28:29.680
It's been a legend since the old days.

468
28:29.710 --> 28:32.480
Back then, the path up here was just a dirt trail,

469
28:32.760 --> 28:36.720
and between the heat, the rain, and the wind,

470
28:37.020 --> 28:38.520
they'd end up arguing on the way down

471
28:38.720 --> 28:39.500
and breaking up.

472
28:42.280 --> 28:42.880
Sir,

473
28:43.140 --> 28:45.430
the two of us won't be breaking up.

474
28:45.610 --> 28:46.660
We're already married.

475
28:46.760 --> 28:47.320
What?

476
28:47.540 --> 28:50.080
Oh, then I must apologize.

477
28:50.120 --> 28:52.840
You're married? Well, congratulations.

478
28:53.020 --> 28:57.040
I wish you both a long life together until you're old and gray.

479
28:57.790 --> 28:59.310
- Thank you so much. - Thank you.

480
28:59.330 --> 29:00.190
My pleasure.

481
29:00.260 --> 29:01.950
I'll get back to work now.

482
29:02.730 --> 29:03.610
- Sure thing. - Take care.

483
29:13.920 --> 29:15.530
Don't pay any mind to those legends.

484
29:16.510 --> 29:17.830
Whether people break up or not

485
29:17.980 --> 29:18.830
depends on the people,

486
29:19.040 --> 29:20.260
not the place.

487
29:22.860 --> 29:23.820
Besides,

488
29:24.410 --> 29:26.080
aren't we soulmates?

489
29:28.960 --> 29:30.180
I wouldn't be so sure about that.

490
29:30.770 --> 29:33.460
We still have a lot to prove in the long run.

491
29:37.430 --> 29:38.320
So you're all better?

492
29:38.350 --> 29:39.120
Yeah, I'm fine.

493
29:39.640 --> 29:41.160
I don't get to carry you down on my back, then.

494
29:42.580 --> 29:43.700
All those hundreds of steps?

495
29:44.480 --> 29:45.280
I can handle it.

496
30:06.460 --> 30:08.060
Whose house are you taking me to?

497
30:09.680 --> 30:11.520
You mentioned wanting to buy a house for your mom,

498
30:11.550 --> 30:12.500
so I brought you here.

499
30:13.480 --> 30:15.420
I could never afford this.

500
30:15.940 --> 30:17.320
I could only dream of it.

501
30:17.680 --> 30:18.740
Just take a look first.

502
30:19.140 --> 30:21.480
If you still want it after these six months are up,

503
30:22.440 --> 30:23.630
I'll buy it for you.

504
30:34.640 --> 30:36.790
Come on, let this sugar daddy show you around.

505
30:39.660 --> 30:44.220
♪Hold my hand and I'll lead the way, my moonlight♪

506
30:44.240 --> 30:48.820
♪I'll tell my grandma and the buffalo you're mine tonight♪

507
30:48.840 --> 30:52.830
♪And my heart will belong to you for the rest of my life♪

508
30:56.530 --> 30:57.700
Pretty comfy, right?

509
30:59.670 --> 31:00.860
Whoa, this is really comfy.

510
31:01.090 --> 31:02.440
Thear, what are you doing?

511
31:02.950 --> 31:04.200
Someone might see us.

512
31:06.140 --> 31:07.240
Now that you've seen the show house

513
31:07.260 --> 31:10.700
and the surroundings at Supalai Tuscany Valley, Chiang Mai,

514
31:10.720 --> 31:11.950
what do you think?

515
31:11.980 --> 31:15.360
Do you feel the design and living space meet your family's needs?

516
31:15.380 --> 31:17.120
It absolutely fits what we're looking for.

517
31:17.460 --> 31:18.840
I'll bring my mom to see it sometime.

518
31:21.250 --> 31:23.530
I bet my mom would love this room.

519
31:23.660 --> 31:24.620
The living room.

520
31:28.010 --> 31:29.710
Should we bring her here to see it?

521
31:30.330 --> 31:31.580
Whoa, right now?

522
31:39.920 --> 31:41.900
I'm trying to see if we could do this.

523
31:42.960 --> 31:44.560
The couch is quite spacious, though.

524
31:52.410 --> 31:54.210
Alright, Khaomao. How do I cut this?

525
31:55.750 --> 31:57.490
To cut vegetables, you start from the tips.

526
31:57.510 --> 31:58.950
Use only the tender parts!

527
31:59.230 --> 32:01.130
- Cut them into bite-sized pieces. - Is this about right?

528
32:01.240 --> 32:03.320
That's too small. Make it bigger.

529
32:03.330 --> 32:03.940
Okay.

530
32:03.940 --> 32:05.430
- Don't be so harsh. - Oh.

531
32:05.460 --> 32:05.940
How's this?

532
32:05.940 --> 32:07.420
- Yeah, that's good. - Okay.

533
32:08.950 --> 32:09.500
Like this?

534
32:09.520 --> 32:11.090
- Yes, exactly. - Okay.

535
32:11.120 --> 32:12.010
That part's not tender.

536
32:12.170 --> 32:14.180
- Yeah, only the tips. - Wait, we're not using this at all?

537
32:14.340 --> 32:15.180
Only the tips.

538
32:15.720 --> 32:16.770
You keep forgetting your place.

539
32:16.930 --> 32:18.380
You're gonna get fired.

540
32:18.410 --> 32:19.960
- He's Lady's son! - Oh, right.

541
32:32.470 --> 32:34.510
Okay, the veggies are in. What's next?

542
32:34.540 --> 32:36.080
I'll let Khaopuk cut the shallots...

543
32:36.290 --> 32:37.810
Khaopuk, let me do it myself.

544
32:37.850 --> 32:38.680
- Sorry? - Give it to me.

545
32:38.700 --> 32:39.260
Oh...

546
32:39.860 --> 32:40.760
Be my guest.

547
32:42.480 --> 32:43.080
Do I cut it?

548
32:43.100 --> 32:44.400
- Yes. - Do we need much more?

549
32:44.420 --> 32:46.500
Obviously, we're making a huge portion.

550
32:47.140 --> 32:48.920
Right, and make them smaller.

551
32:49.670 --> 32:51.030
Cut them evenly,

552
32:51.060 --> 32:52.880
or they won't cook at the same time.

553
32:57.480 --> 32:58.540
Watch your tone.

554
32:58.570 --> 32:59.520
What are you doing, Thear?

555
32:59.550 --> 33:00.100
Whoa!

556
33:00.120 --> 33:01.280
Hey, hey!

557
33:01.840 --> 33:03.690
I told you not to come down yet.

558
33:03.720 --> 33:05.190
Now the surprise is ruined.

559
33:05.820 --> 33:06.990
Why are you in the kitchen?

560
33:07.320 --> 33:09.310
Aren't you afraid of your luck tanking like last time?

561
33:09.870 --> 33:10.770
I am,

562
33:11.020 --> 33:11.850
but...

563
33:12.220 --> 33:13.840
I'd rather cook something for you.

564
33:16.410 --> 33:17.610
So what are you making?

565
33:19.020 --> 33:20.490
Tamarind, vegetables...

566
33:21.020 --> 33:22.330
Are you making jor pak kad?

567
33:23.300 --> 33:25.700
Wow, that's my favorite whenever I'm sick.

568
33:26.110 --> 33:27.700
So you know how to cook Northern food now?

569
33:27.770 --> 33:29.190
To be honest, I don't,

570
33:29.260 --> 33:31.880
but I had Khaomao and Khaopuk teach me.

571
33:32.540 --> 33:34.580
I did all the seasoning, though.

572
33:35.100 --> 33:36.920
Not sure if it'll be to your taste.

573
33:37.500 --> 33:38.910
Then let me do the honors and taste it.

574
33:45.100 --> 33:46.880
So, does it look appetizing?

575
33:46.900 --> 33:47.700
It does.

576
33:49.020 --> 33:50.640
- Careful, it's hot. - Got it.

577
33:52.420 --> 33:53.420
They were gone for a whole month,

578
33:53.440 --> 33:55.300
and now they're even more in love.

579
33:55.950 --> 33:58.310
I thought Lady was about to get a new son-in-law.

580
33:58.330 --> 34:00.650
- Goodness! - Careful, it's hot.

581
34:01.800 --> 34:03.480
No need for the palm sugar anymore.

582
34:03.500 --> 34:04.650
- So sweet. - Watch out!

583
34:04.670 --> 34:06.260
They're so in love.

584
34:10.280 --> 34:11.350
Looking good.

585
34:35.710 --> 34:36.370
Poof!

586
34:37.560 --> 34:38.250
Did that help?

587
34:38.640 --> 34:39.880
- It feels better now. - Hey!

588
34:41.610 --> 34:42.490
I don't think that was enough.

589
34:43.300 --> 34:45.030
I have a special remedy. Want to try it?

590
34:45.350 --> 34:46.710
A special remedy? Where is it?

591
34:53.510 --> 34:54.280
Feeling better?

592
34:54.740 --> 34:56.630
Oh, that look tells me that wasn't enough.

593
34:57.390 --> 34:58.800
I think you need some more.

594
35:04.890 --> 35:06.810
It's actually working.

595
35:07.360 --> 35:08.500
Might need a little more.

596
35:13.070 --> 35:14.670
My hand is what's hurting, not my cheek!

597
35:16.650 --> 35:18.310
But did it work?

598
35:22.640 --> 35:23.930
Come to think of it,

599
35:24.490 --> 35:25.990
ever since we got married,

600
35:27.190 --> 35:28.770
my luck has gone downhill.

601
35:30.840 --> 35:32.560
First I got drugged,

602
35:32.950 --> 35:34.160
then I fell down the stairs,

603
35:34.450 --> 35:35.350
got shot,

604
35:35.380 --> 35:37.220
and now I got scalded.

605
35:38.880 --> 35:40.990
Looks like your bad luck finally wore off.

606
35:41.490 --> 35:42.870
I'm the one stuck with it now.

607
35:45.550 --> 35:46.350
It's all red.

608
35:46.900 --> 35:48.470
I'm sure that's not it.

609
35:48.740 --> 35:51.200
It's probably just a coincidence.

610
35:59.440 --> 36:00.920
Oh, my God!

611
36:01.070 --> 36:01.730
Mungkorn!

612
36:04.190 --> 36:05.400
Whoa, whoa!

613
36:08.480 --> 36:09.230
What's wrong?

614
36:09.700 --> 36:10.850
I stepped on a lit incense stick.

615
36:18.700 --> 36:19.440
You bastards!

616
36:22.500 --> 36:23.120
Hey...

617
36:25.750 --> 36:26.480
Mungkorn!

618
36:39.120 --> 36:42.160
(Mother Tongnuan's Shrine)

619
36:42.990 --> 36:43.840
Excuse me.

620
36:46.670 --> 36:47.770
Good afternoon, Mother.

621
36:51.040 --> 36:52.030
See?

622
36:52.660 --> 36:55.890
I knew you'd eventually come back to me.

623
36:56.240 --> 36:58.090
You knew this was going to happen, didn't you?

624
37:00.020 --> 37:01.400
I'm just an oracle.

625
37:02.340 --> 37:04.370
How could I possibly read your mind?

626
37:05.450 --> 37:07.310
Ask whatever it is you want to know.

627
37:10.200 --> 37:11.730
Since we got married,

628
37:12.040 --> 37:13.440
my luck has actually been improving,

629
37:14.440 --> 37:17.400
but why is it Mungkorn who's having all the bad luck instead?

630
37:18.880 --> 37:21.740
Why else do you think it's called soul-binding?

631
37:22.460 --> 37:25.830
Once you've made your vows,

632
37:26.410 --> 37:30.640
your lives will counterbalance each other like a pair of scales.

633
37:32.490 --> 37:33.660
When one rises,

634
37:35.940 --> 37:37.350
the other shall fall.

635
37:43.120 --> 37:44.840
Why didn't you tell me this from the beginning?

636
37:45.360 --> 37:48.820
I told you already. You are meant to live as one.

637
37:49.150 --> 37:52.030
Yet you have heeded none of my words.

638
37:52.150 --> 37:54.580
The heaven and earth do not acknowledge your love.

639
37:54.960 --> 37:56.380
Don't you dare blame me.

640
38:34.300 --> 38:36.390
Good morning, Thear.

641
38:52.820 --> 38:54.650
Did you see the gardener next door?

642
38:54.680 --> 38:55.490
Why? What is it?

643
38:55.680 --> 38:57.600
I really have to hand it to the boss.

644
38:57.630 --> 38:58.210
Yeah?

645
38:58.230 --> 38:58.960
Short, but...

646
38:58.980 --> 39:00.860
Oh! Good morning, Mr. Mungkorn.

647
39:00.880 --> 39:02.030
- Good morning. - Good morning.

648
39:02.060 --> 39:03.230
Where is Inspector Thear?

649
39:03.460 --> 39:04.970
He left in the early morning.

650
39:05.740 --> 39:07.730
To pick up someone important at the airport.

651
39:08.570 --> 39:09.140
Someone important...

652
39:09.190 --> 39:10.170
Someone important?

653
39:25.900 --> 39:27.190
You're here early...

654
39:30.650 --> 39:31.330
Inspector...

655
39:34.240 --> 39:34.840
Belle,

656
39:35.610 --> 39:36.810
this is Sergeant Mungkorn,

657
39:37.070 --> 39:38.020
my subordinate.

658
39:38.420 --> 39:40.120
He was transferred from Mae Sai Station.

659
39:40.290 --> 39:42.390
He'll be transferred back soon.

660
39:42.490 --> 39:43.240
I see.

661
39:43.650 --> 39:44.570
Hello.

662
39:45.130 --> 39:46.060
Hello.

663
39:47.030 --> 39:47.800
Wow, Belle.

664
39:48.250 --> 39:50.520
It's been a while. You've gotten so much prettier.

665
39:50.770 --> 39:52.520
Uncle, stop it.

666
39:52.580 --> 39:54.470
I've always been just as pretty.

667
39:55.620 --> 39:57.230
I really missed this place.

668
39:57.930 --> 40:01.860
Did you miss the place or the person who's here?

669
40:03.860 --> 40:04.840
Exactly.

670
40:05.030 --> 40:08.670
So, are you two going to get back together?

671
40:08.890 --> 40:10.240
Everyone is rooting for you.

672
40:10.310 --> 40:10.980
- Come on! - Are you?

673
40:11.000 --> 40:12.820
What are you talking about, Uncle?

674
40:13.330 --> 40:15.470
You shouldn't be asking me that.

675
40:15.670 --> 40:17.310
A lot of people here are shipping you two.

676
40:17.880 --> 40:19.620
Since he broke up with you,

677
40:19.650 --> 40:22.150
I haven't seen a single person who could handle him.

678
40:22.470 --> 40:24.320
- Only you can keep him in line. - Right.

679
40:25.160 --> 40:27.570
Well, it's not my place to make the decision.

680
40:28.550 --> 40:31.090
Then let me ask the gentleman.

681
40:31.450 --> 40:32.550
The groom...

682
40:32.570 --> 40:34.140
I mean, Inspector.

683
40:34.580 --> 40:35.880
So, what's going on here?

684
40:36.780 --> 40:39.030
We'll just have to wait and see.

685
40:39.170 --> 40:40.390
Hey!

686
40:46.220 --> 40:47.330
I knew it.

687
40:47.360 --> 40:48.870
The person you're wearing that ring for

688
40:48.890 --> 40:50.920
had to be someone familiar.

689
40:51.680 --> 40:53.380
Why aren't you wearing one, though?

690
40:54.620 --> 40:55.460
Oh...

691
40:55.760 --> 40:58.470
Well, the time hasn't come yet, and I'm in no rush.

692
41:27.820 --> 41:28.680
Let me see.

693
41:30.220 --> 41:33.560
So it's about ranks and all that.

694
41:53.540 --> 41:54.900
(May you always be lucky. From Saming.)

695
42:34.680 --> 42:35.340
Hey.

696
42:35.830 --> 42:39.340
Belle is gonna stay at my place during the long holiday.

697
42:39.490 --> 42:40.840
It'll be easier for me to take care of her,

698
42:40.870 --> 42:42.660
and we'll get to see each other more often.

699
42:44.110 --> 42:46.640
Who exactly is Belle?

700
42:47.710 --> 42:48.600
She's my ex-girlfriend.

701
42:49.160 --> 42:51.980
She's the one I loved most and was closest to.

702
42:52.650 --> 42:55.210
We even almost got married,

703
42:55.520 --> 42:57.720
but she had plans to move overseas,

704
42:57.820 --> 42:58.910
so we had to call it quits.

705
43:00.610 --> 43:02.470
You never told me about any of that.

706
43:04.950 --> 43:07.530
It wasn't in the contract, was it?

707
43:13.020 --> 43:16.450
By the way, she knows about our fake marriage.

708
43:17.440 --> 43:19.210
She just finds the whole thing funny.

709
43:23.180 --> 43:25.190
You seem to trust her a lot.

710
43:26.290 --> 43:27.550
I trust her more than anyone in the world.

711
43:40.100 --> 43:41.230
Let me ask you something.

712
43:42.480 --> 43:44.390
When these six months are finally over,

713
43:44.760 --> 43:46.960
do you intend to keep living with me?

714
43:48.380 --> 43:50.530
Hey, I'm going to divorce you.

715
43:55.130 --> 43:56.530
Is it because of her?

716
43:57.440 --> 43:58.160
Well...

717
43:59.890 --> 44:01.100
That's part of it.

718
44:01.820 --> 44:04.030
You see, we made a promise

719
44:04.440 --> 44:06.750
that if neither of us has found the right person yet,

720
44:07.030 --> 44:09.190
we would come back to each other.

721
44:16.160 --> 44:17.130
I see.

722
44:18.450 --> 44:19.410
So that means...

723
44:20.290 --> 44:22.540
you still haven't found the right person, right?

724
44:24.360 --> 44:25.510
Not yet.

725
44:26.520 --> 44:28.670
I haven't found someone who checks every single box.

726
44:29.230 --> 44:31.710
There are people I'm comfortable being around,

727
44:32.870 --> 44:33.700
but I don't love them.

728
44:34.830 --> 44:36.070
But with Belle,

729
44:36.700 --> 44:38.080
she's everything.

730
44:42.510 --> 44:43.430
Okay.

731
44:46.690 --> 44:47.340
But...

732
44:48.030 --> 44:50.440
you should've figured that out sooner.

733
44:53.300 --> 44:54.270
I mean...

734
44:56.170 --> 44:57.830
You shouldn't have led me on.

735
44:59.350 --> 45:00.880
Look, I'm sorry. Okay?

736
45:01.430 --> 45:02.600
That's just the way I am.

737
45:02.720 --> 45:04.420
It's too late to change, you know.

738
45:07.110 --> 45:09.460
When I said I've been having terrible luck lately...

739
45:11.440 --> 45:12.900
I don't think it's just bad luck.

740
45:14.820 --> 45:16.190
It's downright sh*tty luck.

741
45:20.170 --> 45:21.240
Look, come on.

742
45:21.940 --> 45:23.870
You'll be free in just a little while.

743
45:24.330 --> 45:27.450
If you want to keep staying at my place, you're welcome to.

744
45:27.790 --> 45:29.990
It'll put my mom's mind at ease, too.

745
45:30.350 --> 45:31.410
I'd rather not.

746
45:32.100 --> 45:34.290
I don't want to be a third wheel to you.

747
45:36.610 --> 45:37.650
For now,

748
45:39.730 --> 45:42.100
I'll stay with Nadol.

749
45:49.170 --> 45:51.090
Next time, I hope you realize your feelings sooner

750
45:52.980 --> 45:54.580
so that you won't waste anyone's time.

751
46:11.540 --> 46:13.050
It's better to laugh in a cramped space

752
46:13.820 --> 46:15.380
than to cry in a castle.

753
46:16.070 --> 46:17.610
I'll be troubling you for a bit, Captain.

754
46:19.270 --> 46:21.100
I won't be here for too long.

755
46:22.320 --> 46:25.500
Tomorrow, I'll go file the paperwork for my own room.

756
46:27.840 --> 46:28.890
So basically,

757
46:29.820 --> 46:31.170
from getting married for good luck

758
46:31.330 --> 46:33.070
to actually catching feelings, right?

759
46:45.950 --> 46:47.080
I hope you have a good night

760
46:48.350 --> 46:51.400
even if it might be hard to fall asleep.

761
46:55.410 --> 46:59.190
♪I know you're trying to ease the hurt,♪

762
47:02.990 --> 47:09.950
♪But all of this only makes it worse♪

763
47:10.250 --> 47:13.560
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

764
47:13.950 --> 47:16.980
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

765
47:17.200 --> 47:19.090
♪Just end this, alright?♪

766
47:19.110 --> 47:22.090
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

767
47:22.110 --> 47:24.690
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

768
47:24.710 --> 47:28.310
♪I know what's going on, I fear♪

769
47:28.990 --> 47:31.830
♪Every move you've made makes it clear♪

770
47:32.100 --> 47:35.360
♪There's only one thing left I need to hear,♪

771
47:35.540 --> 47:39.960
♪Just let your lips say it, I'm all ears♪

772
47:40.140 --> 47:43.960
♪If you're leaving, just say it to me♪

773
47:43.990 --> 47:48.800
♪Don't make it harder than it has to be♪

774
47:48.830 --> 47:54.680
♪Just say you've already replaced me♪

775
47:55.160 --> 47:58.980
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

776
47:59.010 --> 48:03.170
♪Tell me it's over, and I'll walk out the door♪

777
48:05.770 --> 48:10.330
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

778
48:11.690 --> 48:13.450
- From this day forward, - From this day forward...

779
48:13.770 --> 48:17.140
may there be no more hardship or harm in our lives.

780
48:17.200 --> 48:21.640
And may we live happily for many years to come.

781
48:25.160 --> 48:29.020
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

782
48:29.040 --> 48:33.220
♪Tell me it's over, and I'll walk out the door♪

783
48:35.730 --> 48:40.170
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

784
48:41.770 --> 48:46.090
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪

785
48:49.280 --> 48:50.530
I think I'm in love with Inspector Thear.

786
48:50.560 --> 48:51.730
It's time to call him yours

787
48:51.960 --> 48:53.350
and take him back.

788
48:54.180 --> 48:56.370
How's it going? Are they doing it?

789
48:57.890 --> 48:58.490
Where are you off to?

790
48:58.510 --> 49:00.120
We're going camping for a night.

791
49:02.840 --> 49:04.330
You're jealous of me and Belle, aren't you?

792
49:04.590 --> 49:06.040
I'm sorry for upsetting you.

793
49:06.070 --> 49:07.370
Can you stay with me tonight?

794
49:12.850 --> 49:16.000
♪Let's stop wasting any more time,♪

795
49:16.610 --> 49:19.700
♪Avoiding it won't make things right♪

796
49:19.730 --> 49:21.690
♪Just end this, alright?♪

797
49:21.740 --> 49:24.770
♪Say I'm no longer the one in sight♪

798
49:24.810 --> 49:27.390
♪And that I've lost this fight♪

799
49:27.760 --> 49:31.580
♪Just say it, what are you waiting for?♪

800
49:31.610 --> 49:35.770
♪Tell me it's over, and I'll walk out the door♪

801
49:38.360 --> 49:42.860
♪Don't keep me guessing anymore♪

802
49:42.880 --> 49:45.920
♪Say it and let me go♪

803
49:45.950 --> 49:49.800
♪Tell me all I need to know♪

804
49:51.940 --> 49:56.260
♪Don't keep me hanging anymore♪
